    {
      "text": "Fine-tuning and the Wilson renormalization group — We use the Wilson renormalization group (RG) formulation to solve the ﬁne-tuning proce- dure needed in renormalization schemes breaking the gauge\n\n**Fine-tuning and the Wilson renormalization group**\n\n*M. Bonini and E. Tricarico*\n\n22 pp, 9 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We use the Wilson renormalization group (RG) formulation to solve the ﬁne-tuning proce- dure needed in renormalization schemes breaking the gauge symmetry. To illustrate this method we systematically compute the non-invariant couplings of the ultraviolet action of the SU(2) pure Yang-Mills theory at one-loop order.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Abstract; 1 Introduction; 2 Renormalization group ﬂow; 3 Eﬀective ST identity; 4 One-loop computations; 5 Conclusions; Appendix A; References",
